    "text": "Under an adiabatic process, the volume of an ideal gas gets doubled. Consequently, the mean collision time between the gas molecule changes from <math><msub><mrow><mi>&#964;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> to <math><msub><mrow><mi>&#964;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> . If <math><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>&#947;</mi></math> for this gas then a good estimate for <math><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>&#964;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>&#964;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></math> is given by",
